# SPEC-LINE.md §4 R-D3 (Module D, branch line-version): nightly DB backup
# via plain cron, as an ALTERNATIVE to
# deploy/habit-assistant-line-backup.{service,timer} for a box that
# doesn't want systemd user timers. Same schedule (03:30, matching the
# Windows Task Scheduler job it mirrors, PROGRESS.md 2026-08-27) and same
# `--backup` CLI flag either way -- pick one, not both, or you'll get two
# backups a night (harmless, just redundant: storage/backup.py's own
# timestamped filenames never collide).
#
# Install (as the habitbot service user; see docs/DEPLOY-LINE.md):
#   sudo crontab -u habitbot deploy/backup.cron
# or paste the one line below into `sudo crontab -u habitbot -e`.
30 3 * * * cd /opt/habit-assistant && /opt/habit-assistant/.venv/bin/python -m habit_assistant.main --backup >> /opt/habit-assistant/data/backup-nightly.log 2>&1
